* halfwave.cir: a half-wave diode clipper: R1 into C1, one 1N4148 across it (the built-in model, no .model card).
* The positive half clips at the diode's forward voltage; the negative half passes, low-passed. The configuration is the
* self-test's answer, pinned (fminus halfwave.cir --self-test without these three lines: 4x, omega(1), candidate 9 of
* 16; T1 -70.3, T2 -79.6, T3 0.04 dB). Every 2x fails T2 or T3; omega3 is one diode's closed form where it conducts,
* so one Newton step is enough.
.title HalfWave
.input  u    in   scale=1
.output vout a
.oversample 4 iir blocks=auto
.adaa off
.solver omega(1)
.target solver=-60dB alias=-60dB level=4.5V freq=3k
R1     in a  2.2k
C1     a  0  10n
D1     a  0  1N4148
.end
